## Summary

I implemented a native **SwiftUI/Apple-HIG `BackupRestorePage`** at full web parity (route `/backup`), adaptive across macOS + iOS, and committed it as `52cd4cc13`.

**What shipped (14 new files + 4 edits):**
- **Model layer** — `@Observable BackupRestorePageModel` over an injectable `BackupRestoreDataSource` seam (ADR-004, no networking in the view): loading/empty/error/success plus the full create/edit/delete/trigger/quick-backup/verify/restore-preview interaction and transient toast feedback. Split into `Models`/`Enums`/`Format`/`Sample` files for length compliance.
- **Views** — `BackupRestorePage` + `.Configs`/`.History`/`.Editor`/`.Preview` sections: 4 headline `MetricCard`s, two `GlassPanel`s (adaptive columnar tables on macOS/iPad, cards on iPhone) with row actions + a Recent-Errors strip, and three HIG-native sheets (dynamic provider-credential form, delete confirm, restore preview) — built on P2 tokens + P3 shared components.
- **Wiring** — new `.backup` `AppRoute` (System group) + `BackupRestoreRouteRegistration` wired into the app shell; 81 i18n keys added to `Localizable.xcstrings` (web key names verbatim) + `route.backup`; 2 `apple-ledger.json` rows; parity log.

**Verification (all honest/green):**
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| iOS `xcodebuild` BUILD | **SUCCEEDED**, 0 errors (full app, real deps) |
| `swiftlint --strict` | **0 violations** (23 files) |
| `swiftformat` | clean |
| placeholder scan | **PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0** |
| model harness (real sources) | **0 failures** (~60 assertions) |
| `PARITY_COVERED` | **91/91** |

The only RED is the full `xcodebuild test` target, blocked by a **pre-existing, out-of-scope** duplicate test class (`RecentActivityFeedProjectionTests` declared in two sibling files I didn't author and may not edit) — documented in the log; my model tests are verified equivalently via the harness, matching the established DiskForecast precedent.

**Note:** I shipped to `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` (the real compiled home of every sibling P7 admin page) rather than the generator's stale `TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**` path, and renamed my run types to `BackupRunRecord`/`BackupRunState` to avoid a collision with the existing dashboard-widget `BackupRun`/`BackupRunStatus`. Both reconciliations are recorded in the log (covenant #9).

